From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] imm32: make a new IME UI window when the old one is gone

Purpose: the text being converted shows in every dialog, not only the
first one a thread opens.
Wine before: the thread's IME UI window is owned by the default IME window
it was made with. When XP's Run dialog closed, both went, but the default
input context kept the destroyed UI window's handle; the composition
updates of a later dialog on that thread were sent to it and lost, and
nothing showed while typing.
Change: with the opt-in, a UI window handle that is no longer a window is
dropped and a new UI window made.
Evidence: in the test VM, the second and third Run dialogs of a session
showed no composition before the change and show it after it.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
---
 dlls/imm32/imm.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/imm32/imm.c b/dlls/imm32/imm.c
index 0b2814d..a6577a3 100644
--- a/dlls/imm32/imm.c
+++ b/dlls/imm32/imm.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #define COBJMACROS
 #include "initguid.h"
 #include "imm_private.h"
+#include "wine/win4wine.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(imm);
 
@@ -944,6 +945,9 @@ static HWND get_ime_ui_window(void)
 
     if (!(ime = imc_select_ime( imc ))) return 0;
 
+    /* win4wine: the UI window goes with the default IME window that owns it,
+     * as when XP's Run dialog closes; a later one gets a new UI window */
+    if (imc->ui_hwnd && win4wine_external_shell() && !IsWindow( imc->ui_hwnd )) imc->ui_hwnd = 0;
     if (!imc->ui_hwnd)
     {
         imc->ui_hwnd = CreateWindowExW( WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW, ime->ui_class, NULL, WS_POPUP, 0, 0, 1, 1,
